		"Cuarenta mil personas fueron a verte firmar y te compraste el coche. Llegas tarde a entrenar, pero llegas: la prensa te adora y el vestuario menos.":
			"Forty thousand people came to watch you sign, so you bought the car. You turn up late to training, but you turn up: the press adore you, the dressing room less so.",
		"El terreno de la familia ya era tuyo antes de firmar nada. La casa la levantas tú, pero el sitio donde ponerla no lo pagas.":
			"The family land was yours before you signed anything. You build the house yourself, but you don't pay for somewhere to put it.",
		"El que puso en pie a tu padre te conoce desde niño. Te recuperas entre partidos como nadie de tu edad, y a él no hay que pagarle.":
			"The man who got your father back on his feet has known you since you were a boy. You recover between matches like nobody your age, and he doesn't charge you.",
		"EL AHIJADO": "THE PROTEGE",
		"BOTAS DE ORO": "GOLDEN BOOTS",
		"PIERNAS DE NIÑO": "KID'S LEGS",
		"El uno contra uno lo aprendiste en una cancha sin red: +4 de regate desde el debut.":
			"You learned one-on-one on a pitch with no nets: +4 dribbling from your debut.",
		"Cuando pitan penalti, el balón lo coges tú: +5 de penales, que es lo que decide quién lo tira en tu equipo.":
			"When the whistle goes for a penalty, you are the one who picks up the ball: +5 penalties, which is what decides who takes them at your club.",
		"Sales bien en foto y la prensa lo nota: empiezas con la puerta de los patrocinios abierta, no en tu segunda temporada.":
			"You photograph well and the press noticed: you start with the sponsorship door already open, not in your second season.",
		"Tienes el teléfono de alguien que mueve fichas: tu agente arranca con la mesa llena y el mercado abierto desde el primer mes.":
			"You have the number of someone who moves players: your agent starts with a full desk and the market open from month one.",
		"El área es tuya: +3 de potencia, y si el 9 está libre en tu club, te lo guardan.":
			"The box is yours: +3 power, and if the 9 is free at your club, they keep it for you.",
		"Ya jugaste aquí una vez y nadie lo olvidó: la grada te espera y la prensa te da el beneficio de la duda.":
			"You played here once and nobody forgot: the stands are waiting for you and the press gives you the benefit of the doubt.",
		"En este vestuario tu apellido ya sonaba: el técnico te conoce antes de verte jugar, y la prensa lo sabe.":
			"Your surname already meant something in this dressing room: the gaffer knows you before he sees you play, and the press knows it too.",
		"Tres trofeos de goleador vinieron con unas CORONA DE ORO. Estrenas un par, sin estrenar y sin pagar.":
			"Three top-scorer trophies came with a pair of GOLDEN CROWN. You start in a brand-new pair you never paid for.",
