		"FICHAJES ESTE VERANO": "SUMMER SIGNINGS",
		"El club no puede pagar lo que debe y un juez pone a un administrador al mando. Hasta el mercado de invierno no se ficha a nadie ni se toca un contrato, tampoco el tuyo. Lo que se pueda vender, se vende.": "The club cannot pay what it owes and a judge puts an administrator in charge. Until the winter window nobody is signed and no contract is touched, not even yours. Whatever can be sold, is sold.",
		"CONTRATOS CONGELADOS": "CONTRACTS FROZEN",
		"Tu club está en concurso: hasta el mercado de invierno no se toca un contrato.": "Your club is in administration: no contract is touched until the winter window.",
		"Tu club está en concurso: hasta el mercado de invierno no ficha a nadie.": "Your club is in administration: it signs nobody until the winter window.",
		"EL ADMINISTRADOR TE VENDE": "ADMIN SELLS YOU",
		"El juez puso a un administrador al frente de {0} y te recibe en el despacho del presidente, con las cuentas sobre la mesa. En la lista de lo que se vende, tu nombre va el primero: o sales este verano, o te quedas cobrando menos.": "The judge has put an administrator in charge of {0}, and he sees you in the chairman's office with the accounts on the table. On the list of what's for sale, your name comes first: either you leave this summer, or you stay on less money.",
		"Tu club está en concurso y vas el primero de la lista. O sales este verano, o te quedas cobrando menos.": "Your club is in administration and you're first on the list. Either you leave this summer, or you stay on less money.",
		"Cobras menos lo que reste de contrato y el administrador te saca de la lista. El vestuario y la grada lo ven.": "You earn less for the rest of your contract and the administrator takes you off the list. The dressing room and the fans will see it.",
		"LA REBAJA DEL VESTUARIO": "DRESSING ROOM PAY CUT",
		"El presidente baja al vestuario: {0} está en crisis y no llega a fin de mes. Pide a la plantilla un {1}% menos de ficha esta temporada, y quien firme cobra a tiempo. El capitán ya ha firmado; faltas tú.": "The chairman comes down to the dressing room: {0} is in crisis and cannot make it to the end of the month. He asks the squad for a {1}% pay cut this season, and whoever signs gets paid on time. The captain has already signed; only you are left.",
		"FIRMO: {0}/sem": "SIGN: {0}/wk",
		"NO FIRMO": "REFUSE",
		"LA ASAMBLEA DE SOCIOS": "THE MEMBERS' MEETING",
		"El juez cerró el concurso y {0} es de sus socios: la asamblea votó la compra a mano alzada, un {1}% a favor. No hay dueño que ponga dinero, así que piden a la plantilla que entre con una acción. La grada mira a sus jugadores.": "The judge closed the bankruptcy case and {0} now belongs to its members: the assembly voted for the purchase by a show of hands, {1}% in favour. There is no owner to put money in, so they are asking the squad to chip in with a share. The stands are watching their players.",
		"COMPRO ACCIONES": "BUY SHARES",
		"SÓLO VOTO": "VOTE ONLY",
		"SOCIOS": "MEMBERS",
		"Los socios compran el {0}: un {1}% vota sí en la asamblea": "Members buy {0}: {1}% vote yes at the meeting",
		"DE LOS SOCIOS": "MEMBER-OWNED",
		"Los socios te pagan lo que te debía el club: ${0}": "The members pay you what the club owed you: ${0}",
		"Tres temporadas después, un inversor quiere comprar {0} y la asamblea lo vota al cierre. Los sondeos dan un {1}% a favor de vender. Tienes acciones: tu voto arrastra a la grada.": "Three seasons later, an investor wants to buy {0} and the members vote on it at the end of the season. Polls put {1}% in favour of selling. You hold shares: your vote sways the stands.",
		"Tres temporadas después, un inversor quiere comprar {0} y la asamblea lo vota al cierre. Los sondeos dan un {1}% a favor de vender. Tu voto es uno más, pero la grada escucha a sus jugadores.": "Three seasons later, an investor wants to buy {0} and the members vote on it at the end of the season. Polls put {1}% in favour of selling. Your vote is just one among many, but the stands listen to their players.",
